Subject: toast: load sonner on demand and keep every toast published before it mounts

What: the toast region imports solid-sonner when a toast first needs it or after the first idle slice, queues toasts until the Toaster subscribes, mounts the Toaster as soon as a toast needs it, and retries a failed import.
Why: carried in the entry chunk, sonner cost every first screen its bytes; deferred without a queue, a toast published before the Toaster subscribed was stored but never drawn.

